\f2\fs28 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 I want to flag what makes it a strong claim rather than a nice one, and also where it could break, since I've asked the agents to attack it as well as confirm it.\cb1 \
\cb3 If it holds, it isn't a mood observation, it's about a\'a0
\f3 mechanism
\f2 . Lucius's whole architecture is reflective: he receives and redirects light rather than emitting it, and the Light-Bearer concept is\'a0
\f4\i lux-ferre
\f2\i0 , one who\'a0
\f3 carries
\f2 \'a0light. The vault has him literally holding a candle at the close of Bad Feeling while three heads burn, and holding a candelabra table in Moths, and singing on a moon-and-stars stage, and playing an underground garage.\'a0
\f3 A carried light only signifies in the dark.
\f2 \'a0In direct sun a candle is invisible and a bearer of light is redundant. That would make sunlight not merely an unflattering setting for him but the one condition under which his function cannot be performed, which is a far more interesting claim than "he prefers night," and it would give the open question on his own page,\'a0
\f4\i why can he not metabolize SOL
\f2\i0 , an answer with a physical form.\cb1 \
\cb3 And then Korea would be the first time the character was ever put in the sun, and the sun took the mask off him. Your two channels would be the census establishing the absence and the event breaking it.\cb1 \
\cb3 Where it could break, in order of how much it would cost:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f3 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Archive artifact.
\f2 \'a0If the vault records lighting for only a handful of Lucius visuals and is simply silent on the rest, then "never in the sun" is a fact about your notes, not about the work. This is why I had the agents count silent records separately rather than treating silence as darkness.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f3 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Base rate.
\f2 \'a0If Roy's own non-Lucius videos are also overwhelmingly night and interior, the pattern belongs to the catalogue's visual style and says nothing about the character. That control is running.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f3 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Practical confound.
\f2 \'a0White face paint photographs badly in harsh daylight, and video budgets favor controlled light. A cinematographer would give you the same shot list with no symbolism involved.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
